<title>USA: ServiceMaster raises annual payout.</title>
<headline>ServiceMaster raises annual payout.</headline>
<dateline>DOWNERS GROVE, Ill. 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>ServiceMaster LP said Monday it planned a 1997 distribution of $0.69 a share, up from $0.68 in 1996.</p>
<p>ServiceMaster said it will pay $0.17 a share on January 31, record January 17. It said it expects to pay distributions of $0.17 a share in the second and third quarters, and plans a payment of $0.18 in the fourth quarter.  </p>
<p>&quot;This 27th consecutive increase in annual distributions to shareholders reflects the stability and consistency of our performance, continued growth, and the exceptional cash flows generated by the company,&quot; Carlos Cantu, chief executive officer, said in a statement.</p>
<p>ServiceMaster is a network of service companies.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
